  "title": "Quotient rule",
  "prompt": "Find $f'(x)$ for $f(x) = \\dfrac{x^2 + 1}{x - 1}$.",
  "answer_format": "An expression in x.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "tags": [
    "quotient rule"
  ],
  "data": {
    "function": "(x^2 + 1)/(x - 1)",
    "var": "x"
  },
  "answer": "(x^2 - 2x - 1)/(x - 1)^2",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Use (u/v)′ = (u′v − uv′)/v² with u = x² + 1 and v = x − 1."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "$u = x^2 + 1$, $u' = 2x$, $v = x - 1$, $v' = 1$.",
    "$f'(x) = \\frac{2x(x-1) - (x^2+1)}{(x-1)^2} = \\frac{x^2 - 2x - 1}{(x-1)^2}$."
  ],
